# Project word list -- one word per line, `#` starts a comment.
#
# Read by two spell checkers, which is the whole point of it existing:
#
#   * Vim, as the first entry of 'spellfile' (docker/vim/vimrc), so `zg` on a
#     word appends it here. Vim reads the compiled `en.utf-8.add.spl` beside
#     this file, which is gitignored and rebuilt automatically when this file
#     is newer -- `:SpellSync` forces it.
#   * cspell in VS Code, through the dictionary declared in
#     `cspell.config.yaml`, whose "Add word to dictionary" quick fix appends
#     here too.
#
# So a word added in either editor is known to both, and shows up in the diff
# rather than in someone's untracked settings. Keep it sorted; `codespell` is
# a separate list in pyproject.toml and does not read this one.

